### Managing Missing, Blank Values and 0 Values 
As noted above, I will remove missing (NA), blank values, and the 0 values in Height, Weight, and NumMeals with listwise deletion. In listwise deletion, I remove any row that has any column with an NA, blank value (defined above as "N.blank" in the dataframe summary), or the specified rows that had 0 values in Height, Weight, and NumMeals. To do this, I will copy the values without any missing columns into a new dataframe.

First, I will verify that the total amount of missing (NA), blank values, and 0 values flagged for removal are a small enough fraction of the dataset to justify listwise deletion. While each category has been assessed separately during Part C, confirming their combined impact ensures that deletion is still the appropriate approach and that the dataset still has sufficient observations for training. 

```{r echo=TRUE}
